  "asr_text": "If the boss is eager, things move fast. It's a familiar hope in meetings and business talks. But in talks about bringing Tesla and SpaceX together, that hope may be turned on its head. You think you've stepped on the gas, but the brake lights come on. Concerns are emerging about that kind of turn of events. Musk supported combining the two companies, calling it a good idea. However, he says the decision should be left to the special committees of the two companies. Don't jump to conclusions. There are still hurdles to clear between he supports it and the merger is decided. According to Reuters, a person familiar with the talks is concerned that Musk's statement of support and the public announcement of the talks could make shareholders look more closely, slowing the negotiations. Support from a big name does not always mean things will suddenly move ahead. Note that this is not a report that talks have already been delayed.",
